    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314-a1">

                <pb facs="0605" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Fort Buford, Dak.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 11,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>To <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adjutant-General</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Department Dakota, Fort Snelling, Minn.:</hi></p>
                <p>Lieutenant Bell brought in eleven men, twelve women, thirty-eight children,
                    forty-six ponies, twenty-two carts, three spring wagons, tents, bedding,
                    &amp;c.</p>
                <p>Most of them are Canadian half-breeds; some of them are the same that were sent
                    over the line by General Miles in ’79. Lieutenant Bell says it is a den of
                    thieves. The meat of the cattle that were stolen was found cachéd in camp.
                    Humanity prevents me from carrying out letter instructions, as the women and
                    children will freeze, after putting them across the line, without
                    transportation.</p>
                <p>Instructions requested. Their camp 30 miles from river, on White Earth.</p>
                <closer><signed>WHISTLER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
